<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador int'l reserves rise to $1.76 bln in Oct.</title>
<headline>Ecuador int'l reserves rise to $1.76 bln in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's international reserves rose 4.2 percent, or $71 million, to $1.76 billion in October, the Central Bank said Tuesday.</p>
<p>In September, reserves reached $1.69 billion, a rise of $164 million from August.</p>
<p>Reserves stood at $1.557 billion at the end of last year, down $145 million from the end of 1994.</p>
<p>-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433</p>
